Avoid std::string::subview in the socket1 parser for GCC 15 (Fedora 43).

Hyprland 0.57 uses the C++26 std::string::subview() when logging a
malformed escape sequence. libstdc++ 16 (Fedora 44+) has it, but GCC 15
(Fedora 43) fails:

    error: 'std::string' has no member named 'subview'

Take a std::string_view of the request and use substr(), which yields the
same view on both compilers. Behavior is unchanged.

--- a/src/ipc/s1/S1.cpp
+++ b/src/ipc/s1/S1.cpp
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ SResponse CSocket1::dispatchBatch(std::string request, pid_t pid) {
             if (i < request.size() && (request[i + 1] == '\\' || request[i + 1] == ';'))
                 ++i;
             else
-                LOG(Log::ERR, "Malformed socket1 request: invalid escape sequence {} at position {}, using it verbatim", request.subview(i, 2), i);
+                LOG(Log::ERR, "Malformed socket1 request: invalid escape sequence {} at position {}, using it verbatim", std::string_view{request}.substr(i, 2), i);
         }
         parsedCommand << request[i];
     }
